Title: "`mlg format`"
Id: "11f4cf9f-7f33-4d0f-8f9d-993a978a06bf"

Text: "`mlg format` normalizes the formatting of every `.mlg` file in the current
collection. Run it from anywhere inside a collection (a directory at or above the
current one must contain an `mlg.json`).

```text
mlg format
```

Formatting is normalization, not a judgement call. It:

- ensures exactly two blank lines between top-level items, and
- reflows inline `\"...\"` text values to the `margin` width from
  `mlg.json` (default `80`).

LaTeX blobs (`$...$`, `$$...$$`, `\(...\)`, `\[...\]`) and inline/display
MathLingua fragments are indivisible: their contents are never split or modified.
A text value containing multiline or over-wide math is left
untouched. Paragraph breaks inside text are preserved.

Fenced code blocks retain their internal spacing and line breaks, including
`mlg-fragment` examples. Markdown list items retain their markers and nesting,
with wrapped continuation lines indented under the item text. Prose around
lists and code fences is still reflowed. Triple-quoted prose is supported too.

It reports `Formatted N files`, or `Nothing to format` when everything was
already canonical. If `mlg.json` still uses the old `print_margin` key, the
command aborts rather than reformatting to the default width, since that would
rewrap exactly the files whose author had chosen a narrower margin.

`mlg check` runs this same formatting first unless the config sets
`\"formatOnCheck\": false`."
Id: "3e713a2d-b8f5-4220-bfa3-00263f1abdbd"
